# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Django — any SQLite database, whatever it is named, and its journal.
# Wildcarded because a server copy is easily called something else
# (db.prod.sqlite3, backup.sqlite3) and must never be committed.
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-journal

# Environment variables
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Uploaded media — never commit anything a user or admin uploaded.
#
# Leading **/ on purpose. MEDIA_ROOT is auction_site/media/, and a pattern with
# a slash inside it is anchored to this file's directory, so the previous
# "media/listings/*" only ever matched a media/ folder at the repository root —
# which does not exist. Nothing had been committed yet, but every listing photo
# and site image sat there as an untracked file waiting to be swept into a
# commit by an absent-minded "git add .".
#
# The directory itself is matched at any depth, so this keeps working if the
# project layout moves, and no per-upload_to line is needed when a new image
# field is added.
**/media/


# Archives
*.zip

# Editor / IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/

# Prompt notes
addon_prompts_final.md
addon_prompts_final_v2.md
